+# Browser Cucumber inspection
+
+This notes the current Playwright/Cucumber state before implementation of the
+browser automation slices in iteration 006.
+
+## Shared feature inventory
+
+- `acceptance-tests/features/homepage.feature`
+  - 1 scenario.
+  - Browser steps already exist for both steps.
+- `acceptance-tests/features/member_message_deliverability.feature`
+  - 7 scenarios.
+  - No browser JavaScript step definitions currently cover its background,
+    message-send, delivery assertion, webhook/status, or receipt-status steps.
+- `acceptance-tests/features/operator_email_deliverability.feature`
+  - 3 scenarios.
+  - No browser JavaScript step definitions currently cover its background,
+    status-report, or operator assertion steps.
+  - It is not currently tagged `@todo-web`, so the later browser partition task
+    must address tagging/selection without weakening the domain runner.
+
+## Browser harness inventory
+
+- `acceptance-tests/package.json`
+  - `npm test` runs `cucumber-js`.
+  - `npm run test:headed` runs `HEADLESS=false cucumber-js`.
+- `acceptance-tests/cucumber.js`
+  - Runs all `features/**/*.feature`.
+  - Requires `features/support/**/*.js` and
+    `features/step_definitions/**/*.js`.
+  - Has no default tag expression yet, so `@todo-web` is not excluded.
+- `acceptance-tests/features/support/world.js`
+  - Creates a Playwright Chromium browser and page for each scenario.
+  - Uses `BASE_URL` or `http://localhost:4000`.
+  - Does not prepare the test database, start Phoenix, wait for HTTP readiness,
+    collect Phoenix logs, or distinguish startup/database/webhook/projection
+    diagnostics.
+- `acceptance-tests/features/step_definitions/homepage_steps.js`
+  - Implements:
+    - `When I visit the homepage`
+    - `Then I should see the Memba homepage`
+
+## Existing Phoenix/browser surface
+
+The prerequisite member-facing app surface is present:
+
+- Browser routes:
+  - `GET /`
+  - `LIVE /clubs`
+  - `LIVE /clubs/:club_id`
+  - `LIVE /messages/:message_id`
+- Webhook route:
+  - `POST /webhooks/postmark`
+- Stable UI affordances available to browser steps:
+  - Clubs index: `aria-label="Create a club"`, `Club name`,
+    `Create club`, `data-testid="club-row"`, `data-testid="club-link"`.
+  - Club show: `Create a person`, `Person name`, `Person email`,
+    `Add a member`, `Person to add as member`, `Send a club message`,
+    `Message sender`, `Message subject`, `Message body`,
+    `data-testid="person-row"`, `data-testid="member-row"`,
+    `data-testid="message-row"`, `data-testid="message-link"`.
+  - Message show: `data-testid="addressed-recipient"`,
+    `data-testid="delivery-record"`, `data-testid="delivery-status"`,
+    `data-testid="member-receipt"`, `data-testid="receipt-status"`,
+    recipient/delivery IDs exposed as data attributes.
+- Current message show renders projected deliveries/receipts at mount time only;
+  later status steps will need browser-level refresh/polling or another
+  observable wait strategy after webhook submission.
+
+## Browser step coverage gaps
+
+`cd acceptance-tests && npm test -- --dry-run` reports the current browser
+Cucumber coverage as:
+
+- 11 scenarios discovered.
+- 1 homepage scenario has matching step definitions and is skipped by dry-run.
+- 10 scenarios have undefined steps.
+- 92 total steps, 90 undefined and 2 skipped.
+
+Unique browser step groups still needed for member-facing coverage:
+
+- Membership setup:
+  - `Kootenay Mountaineering Club is a club`
+  - `Nelson Paddling Club is a club`
+  - `Alice, Bob, and Carol are people`
+  - `Pat is a person`
+  - `Alice, Bob, and Carol are members of Kootenay Mountaineering Club`
+  - `Pat is a member of Nelson Paddling Club`
+- Message creation:
+  - `{member} sends the message {subject} to Kootenay Mountaineering Club members`
+  - `{member} has sent the message {subject} to Kootenay Mountaineering Club members`
+- Message assertions:
+  - `the message should be addressed to Alice, Bob, and Carol`
+  - `the message should not be addressed to Pat`
+  - `each addressed member should have a separate delivery record`
+  - `each delivery should be sent through the email provider`
+  - `{member}'s receipt status for {subject} should be {status}`
+- Webhook/status interactions:
+  - `{member}'s email for {subject} is reported as delivered`
+  - `{member}'s email for {subject} has been reported as delivered`
+  - `{member}'s email for {subject} is reported as delayed because {reason}`
+  - `{member}'s email for {subject} is reported as bounced because {reason}`
+  - `{member}'s email for {subject} is reported as a spam complaint because {reason}`
+  - `{member} opens the email for {subject}`
+
+Operator-only gaps should remain outside the default browser run until the
+operator browser slice:
+
+- `operators should see {member}'s delivery for {subject} as {status}`
+- `operators should see {member}'s delivery reason {reason}`
+
+## Domain runner inventory
+
+- The Elixir/domain Cucumber configuration in `web/config/test.exs` points to
+  `../acceptance-tests/features/**/*.feature` and has no tag filter.
+- `web/test/features/cucumber_configuration_test.exs` explicitly exercises all
+  member message scenarios and all operator email deliverability scenarios.
+- Domain step definitions already cover the shared membership, messaging,
+  status, receipt, and operator steps in
+  `web/test/features/step_definitions/*.exs`.
+
+## ADR conformance
+
+- ADR 0003: the shared feature files remain abstract product specifications;
+  the browser gaps can be filled with JavaScript step definitions without
+  changing scenario language.
+- ADR 0010: the Elixir/domain path continues to read the shared feature files
+  from `acceptance-tests/features/**/*.feature`.
+- ADR 0013: PhoenixTest remains the domain/web-test helper choice inside the
+  Phoenix test suite; this inspection does not alter that architecture.
